Subject: Hide "Download New Molecules" when KNewStuff is not allowed

The molecule viewer's button opens a KNSWidgets::Dialog directly, so it
stays visible under [KDE Action Restrictions] ghns=false and opens a dialog
that only says it is not allowed. The button now takes the visibility
KNewStuff's own buttons take from the same kiosk check.

--- a/src/tools/moleculeview.cpp
+++ b/src/tools/moleculeview.cpp
@@ -16,6 +16,7 @@
 #include <QFileInfo>
 #include <QUrl>
 
+#include <KAuthorized>
 #include <KIO/FileCopyJob>
 #include <KIO/Job>
 #include <KJob>
@@ -66,6 +67,7 @@
     KGuiItem::assign(user1Button, KGuiItem(i18n("Load Molecule")));
 
     KGuiItem::assign(user2Button, KGuiItem(i18n("Download New Molecules")));
+    user2Button->setVisible(KAuthorized::authorize(KAuthorized::GHNS));
 
     KGuiItem::assign(user3Button, KGuiItem(i18n("Save Molecule")));
 
